  "notes": "Near-complete 0-100; romanized forms from shalusharma (colloquial western-India-leaning transliteration) cross-checked against preply and Wikipedia (Bengali numerals). শূন্য also 'sunnyo'. 20 also 'কুড়ি' (kuri, traditional/colloquial), 6 also 'ছ'. Fractions are cognate with Hindi (dedh~ḍer 1.5, dhai~arai 2.5, sawa~sowa 1.25, paune~pone 3/4, saade~sare +1/2 for units >= 3). Verify with a native speaker. Indian numbering uses lakh/crore."
